              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for to lift, then the Hindi for to tell."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दिखाना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिखाना — dikhānā — \"to show\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिखाना (dikhānā) is the causing form of देखना, \"to see\": to show is to make someone see. CDIAL traces the verb to a reconstructed dṛkṣati, \"sees\" (CDIAL 6507)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
